  "notes": "Melody-first progressive house that mutated into folk-and-country-fused EDM. The formula is documented almost as a parameter list: his early work is \"based on four-chord structures, sub-bass and simple synth melodies\", so the harmony is a fixed four-chord loop, the bass is a sub foundation at 0.95 roots rather than a moving line, and the melody carries everything — a low-density, singable, arch-weighted lead, \"soaring synths and keening melodies\", with the drop's melody functioning as the chorus. The *True*-era turn \"adds blues, folk and country harmony (dominant-7ths, plagal cadences) to that frame\", which is the IV-I plagal family and a seventh weight well above the lane's. The kit is the progressive-house one — kick on all four, clap on 2&4, offbeat open hats — with intensity built by \"the regular addition and subtraction of layers of sound\" over 4-, 8- and 16-bar phrases, and on *True* \"the kit is joined by live-feel stomps, claps and folk percussion\", which is the snap/tambourine/perc bed at 2-5 hits a bar. He self-taught in FL Studio. ⚠ The tempo is from the sub-genre convention by the entry's own statement. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all velocities, densities, probabilities and registers.",
